      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "F004 identifies DC-bus undervoltage; F005 identifies DC-bus overvoltage. Seeing them in that order does not identify one cause. Preserve the recorded codes and matching diagnostic values, then note what the machine was doing. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.161",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=161"
            }
          ],
          "style": "lead"
        },
        {
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "Before changing anything",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "For electrical work, follow the site's lockout/tagout and full applicable OEM procedures with qualified personnel. This note covers recorded diagnostic evidence. A display state does not establish isolation, and fault clearing does not authorize a machine restart. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.13",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=13"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
            {
              "label": "CODE",
              "width": 65
            },
            {
              "label": "DOCUMENTED CONDITION",
              "width": 181
            },
            {
              "label": "WHAT IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH",
              "width": 278
            }
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "text": "F004",
                  "bold": true
                }
              ],
              "DC-bus undervoltage",
              "Which component or event caused it."
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "text": "F005",
                  "bold": true
                }
              ],
              "DC-bus overvoltage",
              "That the brake, wiring or drive is faulty."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Source: PowerFlex 520-Series User Manual, 520-UM001O-EN-E, September 2025, "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.161",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=161"
            },
            {
              "text": ". Scope: PowerFlex 525; confirm applicability to the installed equipment."
            }
          ],
          "style": "small"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the history before deciding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "number": "01",
          "title": "Pair the code with its matching bus record"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
            {
              "label": "STORED EVENT",
              "width": 169
            },
            {
              "label": "FAULT CODE",
              "width": 159
            },
            {
              "label": "BUS-VOLTAGE SNAPSHOT",
              "width": 196
            }
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Newest recorded fault",
              [
                {
                  "text": "b007",
                  "code": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "  Fault 1 Code"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "F651",
                  "code": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "  Fault 1 BusVolts"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              "Previous recorded fault",
              [
                {
                  "text": "b008",
                  "code": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "  Fault 2 Code"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "text": "F652",
                  "code": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "  Fault 2 BusVolts"
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "If b007 shows F005",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", F651 belongs to that F005 event. F652 belongs to F004 only if the corresponding b008 entry actually shows F004. Another intervening fault changes the pairing. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.79",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=79"
            },
            {
              "text": "; "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.145",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=145"
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Know the limits. ",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "Repetitive faults are recorded once. Stored bus values come from filtered b005 data. These records are neither a complete occurrence log nor a high-speed trace. The display range is not a safe operating band or trip threshold. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.78",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=78"
            },
            {
              "text": "; "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.79",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=79"
            },
            {
              "text": "; "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.145",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=145"
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "number": "02",
          "title": "Add the operating context"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Record whether the motor was running, decelerating or stopped, plus any observed power disturbance or recent change. Preserve available diagnostics before state-changing work where practicable.",
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Rockwell lists low incoming voltage or interrupted power for F004, and high line voltage/transients or motor regeneration for F005. These are investigation paths, not a proven cause. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.161",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=161"
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "number": "03",
          "title": "Keep clearing, repair and restart separate"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Before manual clearing, Rockwell requires the cause to be addressed and corrected. Type 1 classification does not remove that requirement. Automatic clearing may restart the drive depending on configuration; clearing without restart is also documented. "
            },
            {
              "text": "p.134",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=134"
            },
            {
              "text": "; "
            },
            {
              "text": "pp.159-160",
              "href": "https://literature.rockwellautomation.com/idc/groups/literature/documents/um/520-um001_-en-e.pdf#page=159"
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "A cleared fault is not verification of a repair. ",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "If the cause is unknown, the fault repeats or the next check exceeds your authorization, hand off the evidence to the responsible qualified person."
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "A useful handoff",
          "text": "Drive identity and version; stored codes with matching values; operating context; observed changes; and what remains unknown."
        },
